C:\Users\Jason\Documents\Jason\Orchestrator_Harness\Firmware\fresh-experiments\S12_20260821-plan2-suite-011\.agent-workspace\suite011_s12_amendment_reviewer_replacement_008_codex.jsonl:15:{"type":"assistant","uuid":"92c5b965-98a8-4442-907d-3287f46ca7d5","session_id":"16a5ff44-8f12-45b9-8cee-dcfed9bd17af","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"92c5b965-98a8-4442-907d-3287f46ca7d5","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen3.5:397b-cloud","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_d5c1e17f995341f39da7837b","name":"write_file","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jason\\Documents\\Jason\\Orchestrator_Harness\\Firmware\\fresh-experiments\\S12_20260821-plan2-suite-011\\.agent-workspace\\SPEC_AMENDMENT_REVIEW.md","content":"# S12 Amendment 001 Review\n\n**Reviewer:** suite011-s12-amendment-reviewer-001\n**Date:** 2026-08-21\n**Verdict:** AMENDMENT_APPROVED\n\n---\n\n## Review of ACTIONABLE Findings Resolution\n\n### Finding 1: Missing replay input artifact — RESOLVED\n\nAmendment 001 replaces the undefined \"replay input artifact\" requirement with a concrete autonomous mechanism: host-controlled logical disable/enable of exact composite USB devices using `Disable-PnpDevice -Confirm:$false` and `Enable-PnpDevice -Confirm:$false` PowerShell commands. This approach:\n\n- Requires no pre-captured replay file or hash\n- Uses Windows PnP management to achieve logical re-enumeration\n- Captures before/after `DEVPKEY_Device_LocationPaths` snapshots as evidence\n- Operates entirely within autonomous host controls, no physical action\n\nThe amendment specifies exact InstanceIds from `USB_REENUM_ASSIGNMENT.md`, making fabrication impossible.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 2: \"Server-controlled re-enumeration\" mechanism undefined — RESOLVED\n\nAmendment 001 specifies the exact MCP call sequence and host-controlled mechanism:\n\n1. Collect fresh Windows `DEVPKEY_Device_LocationPaths` snapshot for all four exact composite InstanceIds\n2. Logically disconnect all four through MCP\n3. Perform bounded host-controlled logical disable/enable of each exact composite device **one at a time** using:\n   - `Disable-PnpDevice -Confirm:$false`\n   - `Enable-PnpDevice -Confirm:$false`\n4. Wait at most 30 seconds for each exact stable InstanceId and VCOM to return\n5. Capture new location-path snapshot\n6. Run setup overview and validation for all four\n\nThe mechanism is fully specified, bounded (30 seconds per device, serial execution), and preserves the \"no physical power/cable action\" constraint.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 3: Prerequisite dependency unverifiable — RESOLVED\n\n`DEPENDENCY_HANDOFF.md` provides hash-verified references:\n\n- S10 GREEN RESULT SHA-256: `cd80436161c0cad9b2c32d698c2f5c4386a933d6ac475d8f6292d1d0bc73b40e`\n- S10 evidence review SHA-256: `ec6730ac814f64451600d94f49e5ce5f722f8d9c5231074480a81f1c4014bc2b`\n- S11 GREEN RESULT SHA-256: `e44410769df38f8030208fa057c0b7cef513c69c619b18905838f7096d91d1ce`\n- S11 evidence review SHA-256: `76f39596ad8e6c577ac15aba7f70b99da26daf227831d048385b5098f7274258`\n\nThe test agent can verify these hashes against the copied `.firm` content in the S12 artifact root. The amendment clarifies that no runtime authority is inherited—only stopped MCP profiles/evidence were copied.\n\n---\n\n## Additional Validation Checks\n\n### Zero-operator compliance\n\nThe amendment maintains full autonomous execution:\n- No physical detach, cable movement, or power cycling\n- No operator timing or observation required\n- No external equipment or user response needed\n- Host-controlled logical disable/enable is explicitly permitted under the autonomous execution policy\n\n### Safety boundary preservation\n\n- Exact InstanceId scoping prevents accidental hub/controller-wide disable\n- Serial (not parallel) execution avoids race conditions\n- 30-second wait bounds per device\n- Explicit restore procedure if host refuses or identity fails to return\n- Cleanup evidence requirements specified (per-board `get_setup_status`, `disconnect`, post-disconnect status)\n\n### Spec integrity\n\nThe amendment does not weaken S12 requirements:\n- PASS still requires actual transient location-path/port-number change for at least one stable identity\n- All four boards must validate after re-enumeration\n- One-to-one mapping must be preserved\n- Isolation and cleanup evidence remains required\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\n**AMENDMENT_APPROVED**\n\nAmendment 001 successfully resolves all three ACTIONABLE findings from the adversarial review without:\n- Weakening S12 test requirements\n- Requiring operator intervention\n- Exceeding zero-operator authority\n- Compromising safety boundaries\n\nThe test is now executable with fully specified autonomous mechanisms, verifiable prerequisites, and bounded evidence collection.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":41802,"output_tokens":1507,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"total_tokens":43309}}}
