per-board get_setup_status, disconnect, post-disconnect status, final present-device snapshot.\n\nLet me start with the initialization handshake and setup overview. First, let me create a todo list to track the three requirements plus evidence preservation.\n\nAlso I should check the evidence directory exists (it does — `.agent-workspace/evidence` was listed in dir /b earlier... wait, actually the earlier `dir /b .agent-workspace` output showed `evidence` — yes it exists).\n\nLet me also check the REVIEWER_PROMPT and TEST_AGENT_PROMPT bound files? Those are for the manager/reviewer, not for me. I should focus on the spec.\n\nLet me plan:\n\n1. REQ-001: initialization handshake → setup_overview with four friendly names → validate all four.\n2. REQ-002: capture DEVPKEY_Device_LocationPaths for the four exact InstanceIds → MCP logical disconnect all four → host-controlled Disable-PnpDevice/Enable-PnpDevice per exact composite device (serial, one at a time) → wait ≤30s each → capture new location snapshot → setup overview + validate all four.\n3. REQ-003: per-board get_setup_status, disconnect, post-disconnect status, final present-device snapshot.\n4. Write RESULT.json + TEST_REPORT.md.\n\nEvidence preservation: save raw MCP output and commands under `.agent-workspace/evidence/`.\n\nLet me start. First the todo list, then initialization_handshake.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
C:\Users\Jason\Documents\Jason\Orchestrator_Harness\Firmware\fresh-experiments\S12_20260821-plan2-suite-011\.agent-workspace\suite011_s12_cygnus_001_codex.jsonl:40:{"type":"user","uuid":"db12f2c7-8d25-4817-b4e8-70bf309ae13d","session_id":"3ef6a153-aa88-47c1-a1a0-3966ce4f1985","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_a2snw4f0","is_error":false,"content":"Guarded Hardware Server operating guidance\n\nServer Run identity:\n- run_id: run-20260821T145544Z-1f9ea182\n- started_at: 2026-08-21T14:55:44.057170Z\nThese values identify this in-memory server process; they grant no authority and change after restart.\n\n\nThe server intentionally hides some hardware-control tools at startup. The currently visible\ntool list is authoritative: never guess, request, or call an unlisted tool.\n\nCurrently visible tools:\n- connect: Connect from the named project profile only. Probe, target, and external board-config overrides are intentionally absent. For a deliberate exceptional manual connection, initialize connect_override-plan instead.\n- disconnect: Close the named board session and release only its connection.\n- get_board_info: Return active profile and routing facts for the named board.\n- get_state: Return the connected core's current observable run state.\n- halt: Halt the selected board's core.\n- resume: Resume the selected board's core.\n- step: Single-step and return the resulting program counter.\n- reset_and_run: Reset and execute from the reset vector without changing target security.\n- read_cpu_register: Read one runtime-supported ordinary CPU or floating-point register.\n- read_execution_state: Read one runtime-supported control-flow or execution-state register.\n- find_symbol: Search an ELF for symbols; pass elf_artifact after restart or before same-run flash.\n- read_memory_symbol: Read one mapped scalar symbol (width 8, 16, or 32 bits) from the selected board. `board_id` selects the configured board; `symbol` names the ELF variable; `width` is 8, 16, or 32 bits; and optional `elf_artifact` supplies the current local ELF after a restart or before a same-run flash. For example, call `read_memory_symbol(\"board-a\", \"scheduler_tick_count\", 32, \"build/app.elf\")`. A running or sleeping target is briefly halted for one coherent read and execution is restored before this tool returns; an already halted target remains halted. The returned text includes the resolved symbol and hexadecimal value. ELF, symbol, target-access, read, or restoration failures are reported honestly rather than as invented data: retry with the current ELF, reconnect the target, then retry the read.\n- remove_breakpoint: Remove one breakpoint at an exact hexadecimal or decimal address.\n- wait: Pause for a positive number of milliseconds for one logical board workflow.\n- collect_build_artifacts: Normalize explicit...
